# Compiled binaries
/atlantis-server
/server
/tide
/tidectl
/console
/signer
/-.o
/bin/
/dist/

# SPA build output. Nothing here is tracked.
#
# The line below used to claim a placeholder index.html was tracked, and carried
# a `!` rule to re-include it. Neither was true: `git ls-files cmd/console/dist`
# is empty, and git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded,
# so the negation could never have fired.
#
# The consequence is real and is the documented behaviour rather than a bug:
# `//go:embed dist` needs the directory to exist, so `go build ./cmd/console`
# requires the SPA to have been built first. That is what `make build-console`
# means by "requires SPA built first", and what stage 1 of Dockerfile.console
# does before stage 2 compiles anything.
/cmd/console/dist/

# npm workspace. One node_modules at the root; members may still have their own
# for a hoisting exception, so both shapes are ignored.
/node_modules/
/web/*/node_modules/
/web/*/.vite/

# Go test / coverage artifacts
*.exe
*.test
*.out
coverage.out
coverage.html

# Go module local overrides
/vendor/

# Env / secrets
.env
.env.local
*.pem
*.key

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editor / IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Claude Code local state (settings, scheduled task locks, worktrees)
.claude/

# Air hot-reload (see .air.toml)
.air/
tmp/

# Docker layer cache
.docker-cache/

# Workspace-cache: clones of caller repos resolved by `tidectl codegen --workspace`
.workspace-cache/

# Local-dev workspace manifest; operator-specific path: values
atlantis.dev.yaml

# Dev-loop scratch: `make dev-watch` writes throwaway codegen + migration
# output here as it iterates against testdata/schema/. The path is dev-only
# so the real `migrations/tidectl/` path stays clean for operator forks
# (operators run tidectl plan/approve against their own workspace and commit
# the result to *their* repo at the conventional path).
.dev/

# Local mTLS material from `make dev-certs`: a CA and its private key, the
# server and console leaf certs, and any caller certs from
# `make dev-caller-cert`. Machine-specific and secret — a committed CA key
# would let anyone mint a certificate every developer's server trusts.
certs/

# Local tide cache (in case someone runs `tide` from within this repo)
.tide-cache/

# Schema mirror: `tide apply` with ATL_MIRROR_SCHEMA=true writes caller
# .atl files here so `tidectl codegen --schema-dir=schema` can read them.
# The source of truth for .atl files is the caller repos, not this mirror.
/schema/

# Local IR scratch files
*.last-ir.scratch.json

# Generated tree is NOT committed. A fresh clone runs `make codegen` to
# produce gen/, clients/go/client/, clients/go/pb/, and the per-namespace
# proto dirs under atlantis/. The .atl fixtures, clients/go/go.mod, and
# the hand-written common protos (atlantis/common/) are the committed
# inputs; everything below is derived output.
/gen/
/clients/go/client/
/clients/go/pb/
# Per-namespace proto dirs are generated. atlantis/common/ and
# atlantis/admin/ are hand-written and stay tracked; ignore everything else.
/atlantis/*/
!/atlantis/common/
!/atlantis/admin/

# migrations/tidectl/ is also derived — populated by operators running
# tidectl plan/approve against their own workspace. (See note above on .dev/.)

# Release artifacts. `make release-tide` / `make release-clis-native` write
# tarballs here; they are uploaded by the release workflow, never committed.
/dist/

# tsc --build incremental state. Checked in by accident; `npm run typecheck`
# rewrites it on every run, so tracking it makes a clean tree impossible.
*.tsbuildinfo
